-- title:
--   Gluing morphisms out of Spec S along complete orthogonal idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings in a fixed universe with $S$ an $R$-algebra, let $\iota$ be a finite index type and let $e : \iota \to S$ be a complete family of orthogonal idempotents in the sense of Mathlib's `CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents` (each $e_i$ idempotent, $e_i e_k = 0$ for $i \neq k$, and $\sum_i e_i = 1$). Write $B_i := S/(1-e_i)$ for the quotient of $S$ by the ideal generated by $1 - e_i$. Let $N$ be a scheme with a structure morphism $g_N : N \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, and for each $i$ let $\varphi_i : \operatorname{Spec} B_i \to N$ be a morphism over $R$, i.e. $\varphi_i$ followed by $g_N$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to B_i$. The conclusion is that there is a unique morphism of schemes $\Phi : \operatorname{Spec} S \to N$ such that $\Phi$ followed by $g_N$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to S$, and such that for every $i$ the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $S \to B_i$ with $\Phi$ equals $\varphi_i$.
--
--   This is the universal property of $\operatorname{Spec} S \cong \coprod_i \operatorname{Spec} B_i$ for a ring split by a finite complete family of orthogonal idempotents, in the form of a gluing statement for morphisms to a scheme over $R$. It is used in the construction of the extension of a Néron model morphism, where the relevant base-changed Hopf algebra is split into factors and the given morphisms on the factors are assembled into a single morphism.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_existsUnique_specMap_quotient_mk_comp_eq_of_completeOrthogonalIdempotents.lean

